{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered Rachel.</b> He remembered for her that she handed over her signs to her sister, and that she was distressed — lest she fall to the lot of Esau: perhaps Jacob would divorce her because she has no children. And Esau the wicked too had this come to mind when he heard she had no children — as the red poet framed it: though he did not falter, he schemed to take her, and panicked."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:16.837069589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}